entially unchanged.", "watch": "A late wave of Republican outside spending or a sharp national environment shift toward the GOP could pull the margin down, though not enough to threaten the seat.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Sharice Davids (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Sharice Davids seeks a fifth term in a Kansas City-area district with a modest Democratic lean. She cruised through her August primary and enters the general election with a dominant financial position, having raised about $3.7 million and holding $1.7 million on hand, while Republican Eric Jenkins has raised under $20,000. A Libertarian is also on the ballot.\n\nEvery major expert rater places the race in the Safe or Solid Democratic column, and prediction markets price Davids at roughly 95 percent. No general-election polling is available, so the outlook rests on the district's lean, her incumbency, and the lopsided money gap. Davids has also been active locally, touting federal grants for Johnson County projects.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9826, "margin": 15.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9781, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.979, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.97, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9714, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9784, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9769, "margin": 15.0}]}